---
/** Journal entry: head, language label in all six states, prose, figure, pull quote, previous/next. */
interface Props {
  theme: "light" | "dark";
}
const { theme } = Astro.props;
const fn = `sg-${theme}-fn`;
const fnref = `sg-${theme}-fnref`;
const labels = [
  { marker: "IT", cls: "marker", text: "Scritto in italiano", link: "Read in English →" },
  { marker: "EN", cls: "marker", text: "Written in English", link: "Leggi in italiano →" },
  { marker: "IT→EN", cls: "marker", text: "Originally written in Italian", link: "Read the original →" },
  { marker: "EN→IT", cls: "marker", text: "Scritto originariamente in inglese", link: "Leggi l’originale →" },
  { marker: "IT only", cls: "marker marker--only", text: "Written in Italian", link: "Not yet available in English" },
  {
    marker: "solo EN",
    cls: "marker marker--only",
    text: "Scritto in inglese",
    link: "Non ancora disponibile in italiano",
  },
];
---

<div class="page">
  <div class="g top">
    <div class="lab">
      <p class="crumb">
        <a href="#sg-top">Journal</a> / <a href="#sg-top">Travel</a>
      </p>
      <dl class="entry-meta">
        <div>
          <dt>No.</dt>
          <dd>042</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Published</dt>
          <dd>2026-10-21</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Written in</dt>
          <dd>Italian</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>This version</dt>
          <dd class="moss">My translation</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Reading</dt>
          <dd>8 min</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Comments</dt>
          <dd>
            <a href="#sg-top">2 →</a>
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="con">
      <h2 class="title">Three weeks in Lisbon, mostly on foot</h2>
      <p class="label">
        <span class="marker" aria-hidden="true">
          IT→EN
        </span>
        <span>Originally written in Italian</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <a href="#sg-top" lang="it">
          Read the original →
        </a>
      </p>
      <p class="stand">
        I had a plan when I arrived and none when I left. On hills, trams, and taking fewer photographs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="g">
    <div class="con">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The plan was a list of viewpoints; what I actually did was walk until my feet chose the route.</p>
        <p>
          Lisbon is built on hills, so every walk is a negotiation. Uphill is slow and short of breath; downhill is
          quick and full of light. After three days I stopped checking the map and started following{" "}
          <a href="#sg-top">trams</a>, cats and the smell of grilled sardines.
        </p>
        <h2>A second-level heading</h2>
        <p>
          Body text is <strong>Source Serif</strong> at 20 px with <em>italics</em>, <code>inline code</code>, and a
          footnote.
          <sup>
            <a href={`#${fn}`} id={fnref} data-footnote-ref aria-describedby={fn}>
              1
            </a>
          </sup>
        </p>
        <h3>A third-level heading</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>A list item in the margin of the page</li>
          <li>Another one, a little longer so that it has to wrap around the measure of the column</li>
        </ul>
        <ol>
          <li>First step</li>
          <li>Second step</li>
        </ol>
        <blockquote>
          <p>A plain quotation from someone else sits behind a moss rule.</p>
        </blockquote>
        <pre tabindex="0"><code>pnpm new alps --lang it
# creates src/content/journal/it/alps.md</code></pre>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Camera</th>
              <th scope="col">Lens</th>
              <th scope="col">Film</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Leica M6</td>
              <td>35 mm</td>
              <td>Portra 400</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <hr />
        <section data-footnotes class="footnotes">
          <h2 class="sr-only">Footnotes</h2>
          <ol>
            <li id={fn}>
              <p>
                A footnote, set small and muted.{" "}
                <a href={`#${fnref}`} data-footnote-backref aria-label="Back to reference 1">
                  ↩
                </a>
              </p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>
      </div>
      <figure class="fig">
        <div
          class="frame frame--fig tone-1"
          role="img"
          aria-label="Placeholder figure, 16:9 on wide screens, 4:5 on phones"
        >
          <span aria-hidden="true">[ photo ]</span>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="cap">
          <span>[Photo title] · Lisbon, 2026</span>
          <span>[camera] · 35mm · f/8 · 1/250 s · ISO 200</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <blockquote class="pull">
        <p>A city tells you where to look only once you stop asking it.</p>
      </blockquote>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>What I’m bringing home is a habit, not a souvenir: walk first, decide later.</p>
        <p class="sign">— Filippo, Lisbon</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pn">
        <div class="pn-grid">
          <a href="#sg-top">
            <span class="k">← Previous · No. 041</span>
            <span class="v">Why I shoot one roll a week</span>
          </a>
          <a href="#sg-top">
            <span class="k">All entries →</span>
            <span class="v">Back to the journal</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="g sec">
    <div class="lab">
      <p class="small muted">The language label, in each state:</p>
    </div>
    <div class="con">
      {labels.map((l) => (
        <p class="label">
          <span class={l.cls} aria-hidden="true">
            {l.marker}
          </span>
          <span>{l.text}</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <span>{l.link}</span>
        </p>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
